// madc -i: an entry that is the FIRST call of a function template with a
// dependent return type (std::move: `remove_reference<_Tp>::type &&`) shows
// its value, as every later call does. Each entry in testrepl_firstmove.input
// is std::move's first instantiation for its type (int&, long&,
// vector<int>&). madc showed nothing for those three and only the last
// entry's 144 (B46: the SFINAE check of the dependent return type left its
// `;` sentinel as the parser's previous token). The values are the entries'
// own: g++ 13.3 and clang++ 18.1 compute 31, 72, { 5, 6 } and 144 for them.
#include <utility>
#include <vector>
int x = 31;
long w = 72;
std::vector<int> v = { 5, 6 };
